## Stop KG build from wiping registry ontology

Context: Live scenario 3 failed because SHACL suggest returned 0 shapes. Session logs showed 0 ontology classes with 11 entity mappings. Two wipes: (1) `_BuildPipeline._persist_last_build_to_registry` rewrote the version document from a worker session that can have empty `ontology.classes`; (2) Auto-map `save_mappings_to_session` reloaded a stale session *file* (Generate complete had only updated the in-memory cache) and clobbered the cache. Stamp `last_build` only; prefer the in-memory session when saving mappings.

Changes:

1. `src/back/objects/digitaltwin/_build_pipeline.py`
   Persist last_build via `stamp_last_build`; never call `write_version`.
2. `tests/back/core/digitaltwin/test_build_pipeline_units.py`
   Expect stamp-only persist; assert write_version is not called even when export has 0 classes.
3. `src/back/objects/mapping/Mapping.py`
   Auto-map session save uses in-memory session (with ontology) when disk is stale.
4. `tests/units/mapping/test_pge_session_extras_retention.py`
   Regression: keep classes from session_ref when the session file has none.

